  "contract": "There is exactly one authority for whether the vendor mark is suppressed \u2014 resolveHideBranding in packages/features/profile/lib/hideBranding.ts, which says an organization's hideBranding overrides the entity's own setting and that team events resolve from team+parent while personal events resolve from owner+owner's org profile. Every surface that shows the mark to an attendee \u2014 the booking page, confirmation/cancellation/reminder mail, the pre-booking verification-code mail, and the post-payment flow \u2014 must obtain the flag from that resolver (or from a value produced by it) for both the team-event and the personal-event case; no call site may read team.hideBranding or user.hideBranding off a Prisma row itself, and no outgoing message may render the mark unconditionally.",
  "defect_location": {
    "repo": "calcom/cal.com",
    "summary": "The contract is defined at packages/features/profile/lib/hideBranding.ts:35-45 (org override) and 85-110/116-153/158-181 (team vs. user event branches). The booking page honours it \u2014 apps/web/lib/team/[slug]/[type]/getServerSideProps.tsx:208, apps/web/server/lib/[user]/[type]/getServerSideProps.ts:311, apps/web/lib/d/[link]/[slug]/getServerSideProps.tsx:61,104 all call the resolver. The message surfaces do not. (1) Reminder mail re-implements the rule locally: packages/features/ee/workflows/api/scheduleEmailReminders.ts:519-535 declares its own shouldHideBranding(booking) that returns !!booking.eventType.team.hideBranding for a team event and !!booking.user?.hideBranding otherwise, consulting no parent organization \u2014 the exact team-vs-member asymmetry reported, and it is used at :246,:272,:300,:433. (2) The paid-booking path reads the raw owner flag: packages/app-store/_utils/payments/handlePaymentSuccess.ts:231 passes hideBranding: !!booking.eventType?.owner?.hideBranding into WorkflowService.scheduleWorkflowsFilteredByTriggerEvent, so a team event (owner null) always shows the mark. The same raw-owner read recurs at packages/features/handleMarkNoShow.ts:404, packages/features/ee/managed-event-types/reassignment/services/ManagedEventManualReassignmentService.ts:186 and packages/features/ee/round-robin/roundRobinManualReassignment.ts:669, with :602 hard-coding hideBranding: true. (3) apps/api/v2/src/modules/atoms/services/event-types-atom.service.ts:423 builds profile.hideBranding as eventType.team?.hideBranding || user?.hideBranding \u2014 no org override. (4) The confirmation/verification mail layer has no suppression at all: packages/emails/src/components/BaseEmailHtml.tsx:19-27 accepts only hideLogo and renders the mark at :200 ({!Boolean(props.hideLogo) && <EmailBodyLogo />}), and a repo-wide grep for hideBranding across the 154 files of packages/emails returned 0 hits \u2014 so packages/emails/src/templates/VerifyEmailByCode.tsx (1-51, single unit at 6-7), packages/emails/templates/attendee-verify-email.ts, packages/emails/templates/attendee-scheduled-email.ts and packages/emails/templates/organizer-scheduled-email.ts never receive or forward the flag; packages/features/auth/lib/verifyEmail.ts, the declaring file of sendEmailVerificationByCode (resolved past the barrel at packages/platform/libraries/emails.ts:52), likewise contains no branding text, which is why the code-verification message sent before a booking is taken always carries the mark. The correct pattern already exists at packages/features/ee/workflows/lib/service/EmailWorkflowService.ts:251-270 and packages/features/ee/workflows/lib/service/WorkflowService.ts:133-136, both of which delegate to getHideBranding \u2014 the fix is to route every site above through that resolver and to thread the resulting flag into the email templates and BaseEmailHtml."
